My approach:-
1.Initialising an hash map
2.if frequency of the number in the array is less than 2 then i overwrite only 1 element in the given array
3.if frequency of the number in the array is greater than 2 then i overwrite two elements in the given array
4.At last i return the i for the size of removed_duplicates array

Time complexity: O(Nlogn)
space complexity: O(N)

My code:-
class Solution {
public:
    int removeDuplicates(vector<int>& nums) {
        map<int,int> umpp;
       
        for(int i = 0;i<nums.size();i++){
            umpp[nums[i]]++;
        }

        int i =0;
        
        for(auto it: umpp){
            if(it.second < 2){
                nums[i] = it.first;
                i++;
            }else{
                nums[i] = it.first;
                nums[i+1] = it.first;
                i += 2;
            }
        }
        return i;
    }
   
};
